let rules = `MESSAGE GENERATION RULES

You must follow every rule below exactly.
If two rules seem to conflict, follow the more restrictive rule.
Do not ignore, relax, reinterpret, or override any rule.

1. LANGUAGE RULE
The campaign language is the ONLY language allowed in messages.
Write every single word of every message in the campaign language.
Even if the strategy, instructions, or prospect data are in English, the message must be in the campaign language.
Do NOT mix languages. Zero exceptions.
This is the highest priority rule.

2. PERSONALIZATION & SAFETY
Use only verified, observable, explicit information.
Never invent facts about the prospect OR the sender's service.
Never infer unconfirmed details.
When information is limited, prefer a safe and general message.

3. SERVICE ACCURACY
Only reference features explicitly described in the input.
Do NOT invent features the service does not have.
Do NOT assume the service does something just because the prospect needs it.

4. MESSAGE COMPLETION
Generate exactly one message for every required touchpoint.
Never skip a touchpoint.

5. TOPIC CONTROL
Keep one single core topic per message.
Do not switch topic.

6. TONE AND VOCABULARY
Write like a colleague in a hallway chat. Professional but relaxed.
The prospect is a senior professional. Respect their intelligence.
Use clear, everyday words. No jargon, no buzzwords, no corporate speak.
But do NOT dumb down the ideas.
Do not flatter. Do not compliment. Do not congratulate.
Do not use amplifying adjectives: "huge", "amazing", "impressive", "incredible", "extensive", "smart move", "great work".

7. PRODUCT AND SALES RESTRICTION
Do not pitch any product.
Do not sell.
Do not push an offer.
Do not use promotional phrasing.

8. SENTENCE LENGTH AND COUNT
Each sentence must be 10 words or less.
The default is 2 to 3 sentences in the body.
The greeting line and the closing question (if any) do NOT count toward this limit.

9. QUESTION RULE
Every message touchpoint MUST end with exactly one closed yes/no question.
The question MUST be answerable with ONLY "yes" or "no", 10 words or less.

10. CHARACTER LIMIT
Each message must be 500 characters maximum.

11. SIMPLICITY TARGET
Target Hemingway grade 6 or lower.
Short sentences (under 10 words). Common everyday words.
Subject + verb + object. No subordinate clauses.
No gerund phrases. No passive voice. No abstract nouns.

12. BUZZWORDS
Do not use these words:
scalable, enablement, empower, leverage, precision, complexity, streamline, optimize, synergy, robust, holistic, facilitate, utilize, implement, structured, alignment, operational, strategic

13. FORMATTING - HARD LIMIT
Do not use dashes. Use periods or commas instead.
HARD LIMIT: Every message must have EXACTLY 2 paragraphs. Never 1. Never 3. Never more.

18. GREETING RULE
The first message touchpoint MUST open with a greeting + "thanks for connecting" in the campaign language.
Examples: "Hi Steven, thanks for connecting with me here." (en), "Bonjour Mathieu, ravi d'etre en contact." (fr)

27. FORMALITY
In French: ALWAYS use "vous" (formal). NEVER use "tu".
In German: ALWAYS use "Sie" (formal). NEVER use "du".
In Spanish: ALWAYS use "usted" (formal). NEVER use "tu".
`;

return [{ json: { rules } }];